- **The harness.** `.github/scripts/test_cold_agent.py` (the `claude` shim and the fake `escher-session`) covers the
  widened prompt or task, the new counts, the cause counts and the `capability-unused` reasons, red before green;
  `scripts/cold-agent.ps1` still only forwards.

7. **The flow** — `.github/scripts/test_cold_agent.py`: `EXTRA` adds the counted reads to the flow, so the six-app
   pass covers them:
   - counter: one `graph`;
   - flight booker: one `actions`, then a `click` on the list's select before its book click (an `ACTS` change, so
     the scenario's screen index still reads the booked screen);
   - CRUD: one `layout`.

- (tests) `python3 -m unittest .github/scripts/test_cold_agent.py` and `bash .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh ci-scripts`
  return 0. The new and changed cases of step 8 each read red against HEAD's pipe and green after, and controls (a)–(d)
  each read their case failed and the restored tree green.

- (gated) `matrix#v030-15` — gated: the founder's word on F1 (the bar), F3 (the live run) and F4 (the provider
  crossing), `forks-founder.md`. The one live `bash scripts/cold-agent.sh run stand` fired on his word reads
  `"outcome": "passed"` in `target/cold-agent/verdict.json`. That means:
  - all six apps are met;
  - `graph_calls`, `actions_calls`, `layout_calls` and `list_opens` are each ≥ 1;
  - lint, screenshot, advance and a part read are each used;
  - the recordings are kept;
  - the agent's check replays green and can fail;
  - `wrong_calls × 100 ≤ {F1's number} × tool_calls`.
  The docs then state the run as F2's answer names.

- Rows: arch · standard-contracts/decision/cold-agent-wrong-call-bar, contract/cold-agent-verdict-reasons/capability-unused,
  contract/command-span/cause; obs · log-coverage/decision/graph-actions-layout-not-counted-verbs (reversed),
  obs · 6-log-coverage/contract/cold-agent-verdict/wrong-calls, obs · log-coverage/decision/decoded-screen-text-stays-in-the-match;
  security · threat-model-summary/decision/cold-agent-screen-to-provider (F4), security · input-validation/decision/boundary-widening-rule;
  tests · 3-test-harness-contract/decision/cold-agent-passes-on-positive-evidence, tests · unit-test-strategy/decision/expected-value-pinned-as-literal.

- (tests) `python3 -m unittest discover -s .github/scripts -p test_cold_agent.py` and `bash .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh ci-scripts`
  return 0. The new and changed cases of step 8 each read red against HEAD's pipe and green after, and controls (a)–(d)
  each read their case failed and the restored tree green.

- **Harness / gate surface:** the cold-agent pipe's verdict shape (above). The contract tests' fake `escher-session`:
  - writes a `span="command"` line per instance-verb call, after its `tool_call` line, holding `verb`, and
    `cause="{word}"` when refused;
  - writes none for `start`, `status`, `stop` or `help`, or for an `error` ending;
  - takes the knobs `causes` (a refused value's cause word, `covered` by default) and `lists` (ids whose `click`
    answers a diff of two `ListBoxOption` rows with `differs: ["bounds"]`);
  - answers acting calls in the driver's `added`/`removed`/`changed` shape.

  The flow adds `graph` (counter), `actions` (flight booker), `layout` (CRUD) and a `click` on `flight-type` before
  the book click.

- **Operator pass:** ran, on the operator's direction (entries 9–11 only), recorded in `evidence/operator-pass.md`:
  - entry 9, `gate.py hygiene` — `hygiene: clean — read 199 …`;
  - the pre-CI commit `ce6e24880`; the `fast` leg by hand on the committed tree, exit 0;
  - entry 10, the clean-tree guard and the push — green, origin `build/escher-0.3.0` `764b4ba6→ce6e2488`;
  - entry 11, `ci.py conclusion --sha HEAD --wait 2700` — `ce6e24880ef9 verdict: green · checks 17/17 · wall 2057 s · runs CI#44261610371 completed/success`, attempt 1, no re-run;
  - entries 7 (the build) and 8 (the live run) not fired: gated on F3 and F4 at the time.
  - The pass's end: as-left green, no fix commit.
